  "hypothesis": "JS selectionPoint helper may lose numeric point values used by C OR/subtraction.",
  "expectedBehavior": "OR returns decoded A|B and subtraction (A^B)&A, stored using value+1 encoding; computed bounds track resulting nonzero cells.",
  "observedBehavior": "Exact C OR/subtraction wrappers plus selection allocation/read/write/bounds and rect_bounds helpers match production JS exports for all64 overlap value pairs0..7 under each operator (128 comparisons) and all4 disjoint boolean pairs per operator (8 controls). Entire1680-byte maps and computed bounds agree. JS outputs are fresh, absolute and leave both inputs unchanged. Fixed two-selection Lua stack adapters; shared absolute frame only.",
  "witness": {
    "kind": "production_api",
    "scope": "Exact C OR/subtraction wrappers plus selection allocation/read/write/bounds and rect_bounds helpers match production JS exports for all64 overlap value pairs0..7 under each operator (128 comparisons) and all4 disjoint boolean pairs per operator (8 controls). Entire1680-byte maps and computed bounds agree. JS outputs are fresh, absolute and leave both inputs unchanged. Fixed two-selection Lua stack adapters; shared absolute frame only.",
    "limitations": [
      "Finite numeric value domain0..7 at overlapping (3,4), plus disjoint boolean inputs at (3,4)/(7,2). One absolute map frame; no mixed/relative frame, coordinate conversion, arbitrary bounds, signed/wrapping values, Lua parser, finalization or runtime claim.",
      "Actual production JS selection_new/set and OR/subtraction exports, as used in repository tests and translated callers. Exact C functions execute with a fixed valid two-selection Lua stack adapter and actual selection storage/allocation. No custom Lua interpreter. Input maps and output bytes are inspected only, not injected.",
      "Full map bytes and computed bounds are compared, not internal cached-bound dirty flags. Existing Main-owned selection-frame candidates remain separate and unresolved by these comparisons. Shipped exposure is not attributed."
    ]
  },
